          "be about to + infinitive: the very near future.",
          "Future continuous (will be + verb-ing): events continuing over a period of time in the future. (When it goes into orbit, the spacecraft will be carrying 25 kilos of plutonium.)",
          "Future perfect (will have + past participle): a future event that will finish before a specific time in the future. (By the time you get home, I will have cleaned the house from top to bottom.)",
          "After when and by the time we use the present simple for the future: When it goes into orbit … / By the time you get home …",
